## Why This Is Asked
Tests memory ownership across CGO when a C struct contains a malloc-allocated field. Exercises translating a C struct into a safe Go type and freeing resources from both sides.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory management (malloc/free across Go/C)
- Converting C structs with strings to Go structs
- Error propagation from C to Go
- Concurrency safety with CGO across goroutines

## Code Example
```c
// header.h
typedef struct { int id; double score; char* label; } MyItem;
MyItem* create_item(int seed, int* err);
void free_item(MyItem*);
```

